{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074269-questions-about-mysteries","id":1074269,"title":"Questions about Mysteries","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-06T12:10:41-07:00","id":1074269,"title":"Questions about Mysteries","content":"Hello friends! After a few session playing Mage the Awakening 2E some questions arrised about Mysteries.<br /> <br /> 1. The advancement -reducing the Opacity- is personnal or it benefits all the cabal?<br /> <br /> 2. Let's say you have a room that exist outside of space (Quarantine spell, pg. 179). You could use Scrutiny -focused mage sight- but can you can use Unveiling and Knowing Practices?<br /> <br /> 2.1. If you can then does your success help into lowering the Opacity?<br /> <br /> 3. If a Mystery is made of 2 Arcana (once again, Quarentine plus the added Time effect) and your character only has one Arcanum (let's say that you only have Space), can you unravel the Mystery?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12677-alamantra","name":"Alamantra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T13:11:26-07:00","id":1074288,"title":"","content":"1) Personal<br /> 2) Yes<br /> 2.1) Successfully casting a spell to solve a Mystery does nothing to its Opacity rating against you. While the Mystery might be solved you don't necessarily strip away all of the barriers between yourself and understanding of the Mystery in the way that FMS does. If I was ST and you used spells to gather all of the relevant deep information of a Mystery though I'd drop its Opacity to 0 and tell you that you learned everything you can. If your spells missed -any- of the deep information though, I'd leave the Opacity unchanged no matter how many other bits of deep information you ferreted out via spells. That's how I'd run it though, not how it is in the books. Bypassing Opacity with spells doesn't lower it.<br /> 3) Pretty sure you can't. Though I'd let it depend on how much Time was involved, like if it's Space 4 Time 2, then I'd let you use FMS to learn everything authentic Space part and give you no information about the Time part, then if you learned Time and came back later I'd let you do a Revelation to reveal the Time part. If it was Space 4 Time 4 you'd be out of luck with only Space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T14:40:31-07:00","id":1074324,"title":"","content":"1. Opacity reduction is merely you seeing past the chaff, you can't disperse it.<br /> 2. Certainly. Extra-Phenomenal spaces don't restrict practices.<br /> 2.1. Nothing (that I know of) can decrease spell Opacity, other than waiting for older spells overlaying the same subject to disperse.<br /> 3. Certainly! Some crazy complex non-Supernal abilities might be a mixture of a massive number of Arcana, and needing to have ALL of them would be extremely prohibitive. For example, I could see Changeling mirror-step contacts as including Matter, Space, Fate and perhaps even Spirit (it being a fate contract with the concept of mirrors to allow them to cross space between material foci). So long as you can see some part of the effect, you can reveal the whole. It's just going to get increasingly hard, as mixed spells are much more Opaque.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T15:13:04-07:00","id":1074346,"title":"","content":"The mage sight portion of the SoS development blogs gives a suggestion otherwise in answer to question 2.1. It actually suggests that you can in fact lower opacity by doing actions other than using FMS. Granted, that book isn't out yet, but I would say that yes, you can in fact lower opacity by using spells. That being said, I would personally say that no matter how low you bring the opacity, the last one still requires a FMS roll. Also, I would say that the more opaque a mystery is, the more difficult it would be to lower the opacity via non FMS actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}